 "acc_vs_fused_request_disagreement": {
  "definition": "share of moving ticks (ego > 1 m/s) where the two requests differ by more than 0.3 m/s2",
  "chunks": 598,
  "share": 0.00264
 },
 "description": "Open-loop replays of every drive scored so far through openpilot's unchanged radard and planner, scored against the hindsight-lead oracle with the frozen fast-suite definitions: hard = request <= -2 m/s2 while vision only >= -0.5; mild = <= -1 while vision >= -0.3; unnecessary = more than 0.5 m/s2 below the oracle for >= 0.3 s; missed = oracle <= -1 while the label stays above -0.5 for >= 0.3 s; confident moments only, the first 30 s of each chunk dropped; moving = ego >= 1 m/s (hard_moving / mild_moving: ego >= 0.5 m/s at the episode start). Labels: vision only, acc, acc_summaries (40 m), fused 2.6. every_replayed_drive has vision only, acc and fused on every chunk and acc_summaries where it was replayed (not on second-car batch 2); common_three_labels restricts every label to the chunks where vision only, acc and acc_summaries all exist. never_tuned = every set held out of all tuning (owner held-out routes, the untouched second-car sets and batches, the owner's latest drives; the fast suite is the design set). Groups are anonymised pools; route-block bootstrap, 2000 resamples. The independent recount of acc against fused (pooled_every_drive in second_car_batch3.json) differs by about 1 s of 57 s.",
 "sets": "fast suite (27 replay drives, owner road drives, 20 second-car drives, 3 fresh owner drives), owner held-out routes, the 13 untouched confirmation routes, second-car batches 2 and 3, and the owner's latest drives (10 routes, never tuned on; they ran `fused` as driven and are replayed open loop like the others); 598 six-segment chunks"
}